<hr>
<h3 class=3D"m_8a5d1357 mantine-Title-root" id=3D"id-[BMaaS]StandardRelease=
Procedure(BDD)-1.Purpose"><strong>1. Purpose</strong></h3>
<p class=3D"mantine-focus-auto m_b6d8b162 mantine-Text-root">Clearly state =
the objective of this SOP. Why does it exist? What outcome does it achieve?=
</p>
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"panelContent">
  <p class=3D"mantine-focus-auto m_b6d8b162 mantine-Text-root">The purpose =
of this Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) is to define the standardized pr=
ocess for releasing new BMaaS application versions to target environments. =
This ensures consistent, controlled, and auditable deployments, minimizing =
risks and maximizing service availability and quality.</p>
 </div>
</div>
<p><br></p>
<hr>
<h3 class=3D"m_8a5d1357 mantine-Title-root" id=3D"id-[BMaaS]StandardRelease=
Procedure(BDD)-2.Scope"><strong>2. Scope</strong></h3>
<p class=3D"mantine-focus-auto m_b6d8b162 mantine-Text-root">Define what th=
is SOP covers and, if necessary, what it explicitly<span>&nbsp;</span><em>d=
oes not</em><span>&nbsp;</span>cover. Who should use it? Which systems, app=
lications, or scenarios are included?</p>
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"panelContent">
  <p class=3D"mantine-focus-auto m_b6d8b162 mantine-Text-root">This Standar=
d Operating Manual specifically covers the deployment processes for the<spa=
n>&nbsp;</span><strong>BMaaS applications</strong>.</p>
  <p class=3D"mantine-focus-auto m_b6d8b162 mantine-Text-root">The manual a=
pplies to deployments targeting the<span>&nbsp;</span><strong>BDD Environme=
nt (HND1 and HND2)</strong>.</p>
  <p class=3D"mantine-focus-auto m_b6d8b162 mantine-Text-root">It provides =
standardized procedures for&nbsp;<span style=3D"margin: 0.0px;padding: 0.0p=
x;"><strong>deployment execution, post-deployment verification, and rollbac=
k </strong></span>for the BMaaS applications.</p>
  <p class=3D"mantine-focus-auto m_b6d8b162 mantine-Text-root">The primary =
audience for this manual is<span>&nbsp;</span><strong>DevOps engineers</str=
ong><span>&nbsp;</span>responsible for operational deployment tasks.</p>
  <p class=3D"mantine-focus-auto m_b6d8b162 mantine-Text-root"><strong>Expl=
icitly out of scope</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>for this manual are:</p>
  <ul class=3D"m_abbac491 mantine-List-root">
   <li class=3D"m_abb6bec2 mantine-List-item">
    <p><span class=3D"mantine-List-itemLabel">Pre-deployment checks (these =
are assumed to be completed prior to initiating the procedures in this manu=
al).</span></p></li>
   <li class=3D"m_abb6bec2 mantine-List-item">
    <p><span class=3D"mantine-List-itemLabel">Individual application featur=
e testing (this occurs as part of the development and QA lifecycle).</span>=
</p></li>
   <li class=3D"m_abb6bec2 mantine-List-item">
    <p><span class=3D"mantine-List-itemLabel">Incident response for post-de=
ployment application failures that are unrelated to the deployment process =
itself (these are handled by separate incident management protocols).</span=
></p></li>
  </ul>
  <p class=3D"mantine-focus-auto m_b6d8b162 mantine-Text-root">The procedur=
es documented&nbsp;<span style=3D"margin: 0.0px;padding: 0.0px;">in this ma=
nual leverage existing&nbsp;<strong>CI/CD pipelines, with Jenkins</strong>&=
nbsp;for orchestration and&nbsp;<strong>Chef (chef-client</strong></span><s=
trong>)</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>for configuration management.</p>
 </div>
</div>
<p><br></p>
<hr>
<h3 class=3D"m_8a5d1357 mantine-Title-root" id=3D"id-[BMaaS]StandardRelease=
Procedure(BDD)-3.Prerequisites&amp;Requirements"><strong>3. Prerequisites &=
amp; Requirements</strong></h3>
<p class=3D"mantine-focus-auto m_b6d8b162 mantine-Text-root">List everythin=
g that must be in place or completed<span>&nbsp;</span><em>before</em><span=
>&nbsp;</span>starting this procedure.</p>
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"panelContent">
  <p class=3D"mantine-focus-auto m_b6d8b162 mantine-Text-root"><strong>3.1.=
 Manual Creation &amp; Development Requirements:</strong></p>
  <ul class=3D"m_abbac491 mantine-List-root">
   <li class=3D"m_abb6bec2 mantine-List-item">
    <p><span class=3D"mantine-List-itemLabel"><strong>Access to Jenkins pip=
eline configurations:</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>For documenting the automa=
ted deployment steps and ensuring accuracy.</span></p></li>
  </ul>
  <p class=3D"mantine-focus-auto m_b6d8b162 mantine-Text-root"><strong>3.2.=
 User (DevOps Engineer) Prerequisites:</strong></p>
  <ul class=3D"m_abbac491 mantine-List-root">
   <li class=3D"m_abb6bec2 mantine-List-item">
    <p><span class=3D"mantine-List-itemLabel"><strong>Familiarity with Jenk=
ins:</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>Users must be proficient in navigating and =
interacting with the Jenkins CI/CD platform.</span></p></li>
   <li class=3D"m_abb6bec2 mantine-List-item">
    <p><span class=3D"mantine-List-itemLabel"><strong>Understanding of Chef=
:</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>Users should have a working knowledge of Chef,=
 including recipe execution and configuration management principles.</span>=
</p></li>
   <li class=3D"m_abb6bec2 mantine-List-item">
    <p><span class=3D"mantine-List-itemLabel"><strong>Basic Linux Command-L=
ine Proficiency:</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>Essential for server interactio=
n, log analysis, and troubleshooting.</span></p></li>
   <li class=3D"m_abb6bec2 mantine-List-item">
    <p><span class=3D"mantine-List-itemLabel"><strong>Knowledge of BMaaS Ap=
plication Architecture:</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>Users must understand th=
e fundamental components, dependencies, and operational characteristics of =
the BMaaS applications.</span></p></li>
  </ul>
  <p class=3D"mantine-focus-auto m_b6d8b162 mantine-Text-root"><strong>3.3.=
 Execution Access &amp; Permissions:</strong></p>
  <ul class=3D"m_abbac491 mantine-List-root">
   <li class=3D"m_abb6bec2 mantine-List-item">
    <p><span class=3D"mantine-List-itemLabel"><strong>Jenkins Job Execution=
 Permissions:</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>Required to initiate and manage de=
ployment pipelines.</span></p></li>
   <li class=3D"m_abb6bec2 mantine-List-item"><span class=3D"mantine-List-i=
temLabel"><strong>Sudo Privileges for Chef-Client Execution:</strong><span>=
&nbsp;</span>Essential for applying configurations and managing services vi=
a Chef.</span></li>
  </ul>
  <p class=3D"mantine-focus-auto m_b6d8b162 mantine-Text-root"><strong>3.4.=
 Infrastructure &amp; Tooling Requirements:</strong></p>
  <ul class=3D"m_abbac491 mantine-List-root">
   <li class=3D"m_abb6bec2 mantine-List-item">
    <p><span class=3D"mantine-List-itemLabel"><strong>Operational Jenkins S=
erver:</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>The central CI/CD platform must be fully =
functional and accessible.</span></p></li>
   <li class=3D"m_abb6bec2 mantine-List-item">
    <p><span class=3D"mantine-List-itemLabel"><strong>Configured Chef Serve=
r/Clients:</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>The Chef infrastructure must be opera=
tional and correctly configured to manage the target environments.</span></=
p></li>
  </ul>
  <p class=3D"mantine-focus-auto m_b6d8b162 mantine-Text-root"><strong>3.5.=
 Manual Maintenance &amp; Review:</strong></p>
  <ul class=3D"m_abbac491 mantine-List-root">
   <li class=3D"m_abb6bec2 mantine-List-item">
